Types of MPs
The main types of MPs, based on their shape, include microfibers, microbeads, fragments, nurdles, and foam (Sridharan et al., 2022), as illustrated in Fig. 4. MPs are primarily composed of polyethylene (PE), polyvinyl chloride (PVC), polyester (PET), polypropylene (PP), and polystyrene (PS) (Wang et al., 2020).
Studies have demonstrated that as many as 2000 microfibers can enter waterways from a single wash of a wool jacket, and synthetic textiles can shed more than 100,000 MP fibers per wash.
